# Likeness Looter's "{X}: This creature becomes a copy of target creature card in your graveyard with mana value X,
# except it has flying and this ability. Activate only as a sorcery." On turn 3 Bot1 bolts Bot2's Llanowar Elves (into
# Bot2's graveyard), loots away Thraben Inspector, and pays X=1: the Lightning Bolt in its graveyard (no creature card) and
# Bot2's Elves (not in Bot1's graveyard), both of mana value 1, are refused, and the Inspector is chosen. The Looter
# becomes a 1/2 Thraben Inspector with flying and makes no Clue: it doesn't enter, so "when this creature enters" never
# triggers (the ruling). On turn 4, Bot2's, the ability is not offered though Bot1 has the mana and a target: only as a
# sorcery (CR 602.5d).

